M1. DONE. util_funcs/midi_buf.c/.h, knows only uniform_buffer. Item
    {uint32 frame, bytes}, written in place via ub_push_reserve, byte
    count = ub_item_get_size - 4.
    API: new(capacity bytes)/free/dropped_take [main-thread]; clear(b,
    nframes), push, iter/next, merge(dst, srcs, n) [audio-thread].
    Push rules: frames never go back (moved up to the last one); frame >=
    nframes or a size not fitting the status byte -> dropped; note-on vel
    0 -> note-off vel 64 (the spec's value for devices without release
    velocity); same frame keeps push order; drops counted in an atomic.
    merge: stable k-way by frame, at most MIDI_BUF_MERGE_MAX (16) sources,
    the rest count as drops. Sysex lenient: F0 + at least 1 byte, F7 not
    checked.
    Decoders static inline in midi_buf.h: midi_expected_size,
    midi_msg_valid, midi_type, midi_channel, midi_is_note_on/off - no
    status byte checks by hand elsewhere.
